Classic Cheesecake Recipe 🍰
Ingredients
For the Crust:
1 ½ cups (150g) graham cracker crumbs (or digestive biscuits, crushed)
¼ cup (50g) granulated sugar
6 tbsp (85g) unsalted butter, melted
For the Cheesecake Filling:
24 oz (680g) cream cheese, softened
1 cup (200g) granulated sugar
1 tsp vanilla extract
3 large eggs
1 cup (240ml) sour cream (or Greek yogurt)
1 tbsp all-purpose flour (optional, for stability)
Optional Topping:
Fresh berries, fruit compote, or whipped cream
Instructions
Prepare the Crust

Preheat the oven to 325°F (163°C).
In a bowl, mix graham cracker crumbs, sugar, and melted butter until it resembles wet sand.
Press the mixture evenly into the bottom of a 9-inch (23cm) springform pan. Use the back of a spoon or the bottom of a glass to flatten it firmly.
Bake for 8-10 minutes. Let it cool while preparing the filling.
Make the Filling

In a large bowl, beat the cream cheese and sugar together on medium speed until smooth and creamy (2-3 minutes).
Add the vanilla extract and mix briefly to combine.
Add eggs one at a time, mixing on low speed until just combined. Avoid overmixing to prevent cracks.
Gently fold in sour cream and flour (if using).
Assemble and Bake

Pour the filling onto the cooled crust. Smooth the top with a spatula.
Place the springform pan on a baking sheet and bake for 55-65 minutes. The edges should be set, but the center will have a slight jiggle.
Cool and Chill

Turn off the oven and crack the door open slightly. Let the cheesecake cool in the oven for 1 hour to prevent sudden temperature changes.
Cover and refrigerate for at least 4 hours, preferably overnight.
Serve

Remove the cheesecake from the springform pan. Top with fresh berries, fruit compote, or whipped cream, if desired.
Slice 
and 
enjoy!
